    "B hears the question and builds the answer. Put the small pronoun (me, te, lhe, o …) in the right place. By default it goes after the verb with a hyphen: dou-te, falou-me (enclisis). It goes before the verb after não, nobody and nothing (ninguém, nada), question words, que, já, também, se and quando: não te posso ajudar, já lhe falei, quando me ligam. The hyphen is not on a tile, you add it. A tile in brackets such as (eu) says who is meant; you don’t write it.",
